Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:12:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 088/154] feat(sidebar): backfill favicons for rows with no
 live tab
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A restored or pinned row has no WebContents, so the reactive per-tab favicon
pipeline never produced its icon and the row stayed an empty square for the
session. The snapshot is the only place the browser learns those URLs, so the
push now selects the rows with no cached icon and hands them to a bounded,
once-per-URL backfill queue shared by the profile's windows. A row asks the
tab-keyed cache first and falls back to the URL-keyed one, remembering the
404 so the next push does not pay for it twice.

Icon paths gain a profile scope segment (favicon/<scope>/... and
urlicon/<scope>/...), so a surface showing another profile's rows reads that
profile's cache and an incognito window cannot read the regular one.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 1977833ef0bbe..d11cda29d2011 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -629,6 +629,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:drop_target_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:extension_actions_json",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:bounded_icon_store",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:icon_backfill",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:visit_thumbnail_store",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:edit_focus_gate",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:external_link",
